# CLAUDE.md is committed (it imports AGENTS.md and adds the Claude-specific subset).
# Personal, machine-specific notes go in CLAUDE.local.md, which Claude Code loads right after it.
CLAUDE.local.md
# Both spellings: `venv/` does not match `.venv/`. Until now the only thing keeping a ~865MB
# `.venv/` out of git was the `.gitignore` containing `*` that Python's venv module writes inside
# it — invisible here, and absent if the venv is built by a Python older than 3.11.
venv/
.venv/
Notes
Plans
sage.db*
Payload_Type/sage/sage*.db*
# Claude Code's project directory ships two of its three entries, and hides the third.
#
# `settings.json` is committed: plain JSON carrying the same two guardrail hooks as
# `.codex/config.toml`. Without it a Claude Code contributor gets no architecture gate and no
# retention guard at all.
#
# `skills/` is committed as of 2026-08-11, reversing the original call. It holds one symlink per
# entry in this repo's own `skills/` tree, so committing it means a Linux or macOS clone has every
# Sage skill discoverable the moment Claude Code starts, with no setup step. That was the whole
# point of putting them in `skills/` in the first place, and a link loop a contributor has to find
# and run is a setup step most will skip.
#
# The known cost, accepted deliberately: under `core.symlinks=false` — the Git-for-Windows default
# without Developer Mode — git materializes each link as a small text file containing its target
# path, silently. A Windows contributor sees 15 inert files rather than 15 skills. The fix there is
# to delete `.claude/skills/` and re-create the links, which needs Developer Mode or an elevated
# shell; `AGENTS.md` carries the loop. Every other platform pays nothing.
#
# `settings.local.json` stays ignored, and this is the load-bearing half of the rule. It accretes
# personal absolute paths, private model pins, and hundreds of one-off command approvals — real
# violations of the Publishable-By-Default Contract in `AGENTS.md`, not merely noise. Claude Code's
# own convention already draws this line: `settings.json` is shared, `settings.local.json` is not.
# It needs no rule of its own; the `.claude/*` wildcard below already excludes it, and the two
# negations deliberately do not bring it back.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file underneath an excluded directory, so the rule is `.claude/*` rather
# than `.claude/`: the wildcard matches only the three entries at that one level, letting the
# negations re-admit two of them along with everything inside `skills/`.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills
.env
# ...except Sage's own runtime env, which is committed deliberately. It ships fully commented out so
# it sets nothing, and exists in the repo so a Mythic operator can edit it in place from the web UI
# instead of needing a shell inside the container to copy an example file. The negation must come
# after the `.env` rule above to take effect.
# Your local edits to it will still show in `git status` — .gitignore does not apply to a tracked
# file. Use `git update-index --skip-worktree Payload_Type/sage/.env` if you want them hidden.
!Payload_Type/sage/.env
# Local overrides beside it stay private — only the committed template is tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example
skills/sage-callback-bootstrap/*_callback_config.json
.evals/
.mcp.json
.envrc
skills/sage-eval-gauge/.env.local

# Phoenix observability directory - ignore contents but keep structure
Payload_Type/sage/.phoenix/*
!Payload_Type/sage/.phoenix/.keep

# Operator tool binary drop zone - ignore contents but keep structure
Payload_Type/sage/tools/*
!Payload_Type/sage/tools/.keep

# SSL certificate bundles - exclude from version control
Payload_Type/sage/certs/*.pem
Payload_Type/sage/sage.log
Payload_Type/sage/evals/results/

# Sage durable engagement-state ledger and local analysis artifacts (runtime state — never commit)
.sage_engagement/
.hillclimb/
**/.trajectory/
# Residual guard. The HITL audit writer was removed (model.py `_write_hitl_audit`), so nothing
# creates this any more — but a Sage process still running the older code keeps appending until it
# is restarted, and the file reached 12.8MB. Cheap insurance against committing that.
**/MEMORY/audit.jsonl
.r5_preflight/

# Private durable Codex/Sage contracts, handoffs, reviews, transcripts, and evidence
.sage_history/
